1. INTRODUCTION

The Library Management System is a database-based project developed using MySQL Workbench. It is designed to manage student information, book details, book issuing, and book returning.

The system maintains records of students and books and helps track which books are available and which books have been issued. It reduces manual paperwork and makes library record management easier and more efficient.

2. OBJECTIVES OF THE PROJECT

The main objectives of this project are:

To create a database for managing library records.
To store student information.
To maintain book details and availability.
To record book issue and return information.
To retrieve available books using SQL queries.
To demonstrate primary keys and foreign keys.
To implement SQL joins and aggregate functions.
To understand database management in real-world applications.
