4. DATABASE DESIGN

The database name used in this project is LibraryDB.

The database contains three main tables:

4.1 Students Table

This table stores student information.

Fields:

Student_ID – Primary Key
Student_Name – Name of the student
Department – Student's department
Email – Email address
Phone – Contact number
4.2 Books Table

This table stores information about library books.

Fields:

Book_ID – Primary Key
Title – Book title
Author – Author's name
Publisher – Publisher's name
Quantity – Total number of copies
Available_Quantity – Number of available copies
4.3 Book_Issue Table

This table stores book issue and return records.

Fields:

Issue_ID – Primary Key
Student_ID – Foreign Key
Book_ID – Foreign Key
Issue_Date – Date of book issue
Return_Date – Date of book return
Status – Issued or Returned
5. DATABASE RELATIONSHIPS

The Students, Books, and Book_Issue tables are connected through primary and foreign keys.

One student can have multiple book issue records.
One book can appear in multiple issue records over time.
The Book_Issue table connects the Students and Books tables.

Primary keys uniquely identify records, while foreign keys maintain relationships between tables and ensure referential integrity.

